# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
crafts_have_work	one
members_have_work	one
man_has_work	one
# "work" (ergon) means a craftsman's occupation in P1 and A1, and an organ's natural function in P2 and A2.
# A1 could be read as passing from work as a trade to work as a function Man has by Nature.
# But the text treats "work" as one notion throughout, a characteristic activity. A1 and A2 each join two different claims and do not move "work" between senses, so neither is a bridge.
